{title: We Belong to the Lord}
{subtitle: Romans 14:7–8}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×17

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Who are you to judge another's servant
He stands or falls before his master
The Lord is able to make him stand
So let each be fully convinced in his mind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For [B]none of us lives to him[C#]self
And [B]none of us dies to him[C#]self
If we [D#m]live we live to the Lord
If [C#]we die we die to the Lord
We belong to the [B]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [B] | [C#] | [D#m] | [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
One regards one day above another
Another regards every day alike
Whoever eats does so to the Lord
And whoever abstains gives thanks to God
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [B] | [C#] | [D#m] | [D#m] | ×3

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[B]Christ died and re[C#]turned to life
[D#m]To be Lord of the dead and living
[B]Why do you judge [C#]your brother
[D#m]Why do you look down on him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[B]We will all stand [C#]before the judgment [D#m]seat
[B]Every knee will [C#]bow to the [D#m]Lord
{end_of_verse}
